Implement a water bottle bowling game using Three.js. Use water bottle models as bowling pins and launch a bowling ball to knock them down.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following import map in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/WaterBottle.glb;
(2) Clone it 10 times to use as bowling pins, arranged in a triangular formation (4-3-2-1);
(3) Keep the bottles upright, with spacing of 0.8 units;

[Bowling Ball]
(4) Use SphereGeometry (radius=0.3, dark blue) for the ball;
(5) Place the ball initially 8 units in front of the pin formation;

[Launch Interaction]
(6) Drag the mouse left and right to adjust the launch angle;
(7) Drag up and down to adjust the launch force (5-20 m/s);
(8) Release to launch, and display a force indicator bar;

[Physics Simulation]
(9) The ball rolls along the launch direction, with a friction decay coefficient of 0.95;
(10) When the ball hits a pin, calculate the collision force and push the pin over (rotation);
(11) A pin is considered down when its rotation exceeds 45 degrees;

[Scoring]
(12) Allow 2 throws per frame (10 frames total); knocking all pins down = Strike;
(13) Simplification: count the number of knocked-down pins after each throw;
(14) A "Reset" button (id="resetBtn") stands all pins upright again;

[HUD Display]
(15) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Number of pins down (id="pinsDown")
  - Current frame (id="frame")
  - Total score (id="totalScore")
  - Ball speed (id="ballSpeed")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean
  - pinsDown: number (0-10)
  - frame: number (1-10)
  - totalScore: number
  - ballSpeed: number
  - ballPos: {x,y,z}

Output a standalone HTML file.
